how to migrate off of microsoft and other closed-source software

Microsoft software
For the office suite, obviously LibreOffice, its practically the same, but free. for VSCode, use vscodium. No question there. For github, just use git in your terminal.


Operating system
if you dont want to use a terminal at all: Linux mint is recommended, very stable, looks similar to windows. 
Less customisable, but very good for daily driving. Lindows is also an option (not linspire), but it is far less stable. 
For gaming, we recommend bazzite or steam os, with enhanced performance. a little higher maintainance, but worth it for a dedicated gaming machine. 
if you are willing to use the terminal try ubuntu, or if you want something even more stable debian.
If you want newer features try fedora. Higher maintainance, but very efficient when used right.
If you are a masochist and enjoy suffering, use arch.

